The whole vocabulary in one place. If a word in the docs is unfamiliar, it is defined here.

## The five words

- **Page** — a route that ships as server HTML with no Kit client (`csr = false`). Only islands hydrate. See [How it works](/docs/start/how-it-works).
- **Island** — a component that becomes interactive by getting JS on a schedule. See [Client islands](/docs/islands/client-islands).
- **Lake** — static HTML *inside* an island that ships zero client JS. See [Lakes](/docs/islands/lakes).
- **Server island** — HTML fetched from the server after load; placeholder first, no JS. See [Server islands](/docs/islands/server-islands).
- **Partial** — a server-*chosen* renderable you place like data (`<Region of={x} />`). See [Partials](/docs/data-state/partials).

## Attributes & schedules

- **`hydrate`** — the import attribute that makes an island (or a lake, at `'none'`).
- **`defer`** — the import attribute that makes a server island.
- **`partial`** — the import attribute that turns a component into a server-chosen partial.
- **`preset`** — a named bundle of attributes defined in plugin config, applied with `with { preset: 'name' }`.
- **`load` / `idle` / `visible` / `interaction` / `(media)`** — the schedules. `interaction` (hydrate-only) wakes on first pointer/key/focus, replaying the click that woke it. On an island they say when JS runs; on a server island, when HTML arrives. See [Timing & nesting](/docs/islands/timing-nesting).

## Mechanics

- **Region** — the DOM element (`<ogygia-region>`) the runtime manages for every island, lake, or server island.
- **Runtime** — the ~7.6 KB custom element + router that boots on a Page and wakes regions on schedule.
- **Portable binding** — a marked import whose *binding* is the island, so you can pass it around like any component. See [Portable bindings](/docs/islands/portable-bindings).
- **Nearest-boundary rule** — nesting is decided by the closest marked parent. See [Timing & nesting](/docs/islands/timing-nesting).
- **Dedupe** — the same component + strategy produces one client chunk, however many times it is used.

## Data & state

- **Remote function** — a Kit `query` / `command` / `form` etc., callable from inside islands. See [Remote functions](/docs/data-state/remote-functions).
- **Live partial** — a partial re-emitted over time by `query.live`, morphed or kept-alive in place. See [Partials](/docs/data-state/partials).
- **Transportable** — a class that can cross an island boundary as a prop by declaring `static [ogygia.wire]`. See [Shared state](/docs/data-state/state-context#sharing-state).
- **Codec** — the `{ encode, decode }` pair on a transportable class that says how its instances travel.
- **Wire tag** — the stable identity (`module#Class`) a transportable is registered under on both sides.

## Content

- **Collection** — a set of content entries defined with `content()`. See [Content collections](/docs/content/collections).
- **Entry** — a single item: `{ id, data, meta, body }`, where `body` is a partial and `meta` is source-derived (e.g. `{ headings }`).
- **Source / loader** — where a collection's entries come from: a `{ get, list, ids }` object. `mdsvex()`, `json()`, `blocks()` build one from a glob; write your own to fetch a CMS. See [Live & CMS sources](/docs/content/live).

## Streaming

- **Streaming** — sending server-island HTML down the page's own response instead of a fetch per hole (`stream: true`). See [Streaming & PPR](/docs/app/streaming-ppr).
- **Parcel** — one hole's streamed HTML, delivered as a `<template data-ogygia-slot>`.
- **Shell caching** — cache a route's static shell and replay it as the streaming envelope while holes stream fresh. Opt in with `export const shell = 'cache' | 'swr'` (same config as `remount`). See [Streaming & PPR](/docs/app/streaming-ppr).
- **PPR (partial prerendering)** — the shape shell caching produces: a static shell with dynamic Partials streamed at request time, no client waterfall.
